{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets (excl. territories) and the 2025 population from the census file's own 'United States' row : how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786912299633},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Find the total farmers markets (excluding territories) from the first dataset\n2. Get the 2025 U.S. population from the second dataset's 'United States' row\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to 4 decimal places\n\nI need to follow the xorq analyst procedure:\n1. First, orient myself with the catalog - check for semantic models and existing aliases\n2. Ingest the data sources as needed\n3. Compute the values using xorq_select\n4. Verify using xorq_verify\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog path and available models/aliases.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you find the farmers markets per 100,000 residents using the xorq tools. Let me start by orienting myself with the catalog and then ingesting these data sources."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01EK4BDcjyJHwTkwFXtmAqc8","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01W2HBxctn7nPZkaEpQS55mA","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":309,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8177,"totalTokens":8496,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.001545000000000000